# Machine Learning approaches for accelerating Antibiotic Susceptibility Testing (AST) in microfluidic systems

Master’s Degree in Bioinformatics - University of Minho  
Curricular Unit: Project  
Year: 2026

This repository contains the code, reports, and presentations developed during this project.

## Project Objective
The objective of this project was to use early time-series data to predict bacterial growth inhibition and reduce the time required to estimate the minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC).

## Repository structure
|
├── notebooks/  #(15 Jupyter notebooks covering data analysis, feature engineering, and ML models)
├── auxiliary_python_files/
|
Phase1_ML_approaches_for_AST_Eduarda_Santos.pdf
Presentation.pdf
ML_approaches_for_AST_Eduarda_Santos.pdf
README.md

## Data
The dataset used in this project originates from a PhD research programme at the University of Bath.
Due to confidentiality and ongoing research, the dataset is not publicly available.
As a result, the code is not directly executable without access to the original data.

## Requirements
- Python 3.12  
- NumPy  
- pandas  
- scikit-learn  
- matplotlib  
